# Cloudflare Pages redirects (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
# Source of truth: deployment/cloudflare/_redirects — the build copies
# this file verbatim to docs/_redirects and validates every active rule
# (see parse_redirects() in scripts/build.py). GitHub Pages ignores it.
#
# There are currently NO active redirect rules: this site has never
# renamed a published URL, so there are no legacy addresses to redirect
# (the one historical move — accessibility-statement.html onto the About
# page — is already handled by a generated meta-refresh stub that works
# on any static host). Do not invent old URLs.
#
# Rule format, when one is genuinely needed:
#   /old-path  /new-path  301
# e.g. (example only — not an active rule):
#   /accessibility.html  /about.html  301
